#### Conditional Probability

Note that in this case the only possible outcomes are (\(X=0\), \(Y=1\)) and (\(X=1\), \(Y=0\)) and thus the two random variables are, in a certain sense, maximally distinct; that is, there is not a single state of the world with nonzero probability in which the two random variables take identical values.

